title: 'Malte Ubl, "Design Docs at Google" (2020): write one where the solution is ambiguous and trade-offs matter; a doc that only says how you will build it is not worth writing.'
pid: 79b82187-fc28-4557-a640-b3b90f976161
body: |2-
  https://www.industrialempathy.com/posts/design-docs-at-google/
  Sections: context and scope, goals and non-goals, the design, and
  alternatives considered, "one of the most important". 1-3 pages
  for incremental work. Review can become "a dangerous trap of
  overhead". Update the doc while the system is unbuilt; afterward
  changes accumulate as amendments, and become hard to follow.
  "I tried it out and it works" is one of the best arguments.
